  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "e6ntpb3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance encompasses Public Revenue, Public Expenditure, Deficits, Public Debt, and Budgetary Management.",
        "Public Revenue is broadly categorized into Tax Revenue (Direct and Indirect Taxes) and Non-Tax Revenue.",
        "Budgetary Deficits form the core analytical section of public finance, divided into Revenue, Fiscal, and Primary Deficits.",
        "Deficit Financing and Public Debt are crucial mechanisms used by governments to bridge fiscal gaps.",
        "The Finance Commission serves as the key constitutional body managing financial allocations and recommendations."
      ],
      "id": "ri780jj"
    },
